+# TASK_GUIDE — T001: `tally summary --month YYYY-MM`
+**Date**: 2026-10-26
+**Complexity Level**: C1
+**Risk Level**: Low
+**Priority**: P1
+**Assigned agent**: backend-developer
+**Agent guide**: `agents/backend.md`
+
+---
+
+## Mandatory Startup (Do Not Skip)
+
+1. Read the memory slice in your spawn prompt; `memory/MEMORY.md` only if needed
+2. Read this file completely
+3. Read `agents/backend.md`
+(`PROJECT_SPEC.md` does not exist in this repo yet; this task is a single-file CLI change.)
+
+---
+
+## Requirement (Pillar 1 — Adapt the requirement)
+
+Add a `--month` option to `tally summary`. `python3 -m tally summary --month 2026-03` counts only expenses dated in March 2026. An invalid month (`2026-13`, `march`) prints an error and exits with status 2, the same way `list --since` does with a bad date. Without `--month`, behavior is unchanged.
+
+**Restated intent**:
+> `summary` can be limited to one calendar month; bad input fails like `list --since`.
+
+**Out of scope**:
+- Month filters on other commands
+- Changing output format or `reports.py`
+
+**Requirement Refs**: None (no PRD.md in this repo)
+
+### Requirement Fidelity Gate
+
+- [x] Restated intent confirmed to match the user's request (Supervisor)
+- [x] Domain terms align (no glossary in repo)
+- [x] Every Acceptance Criterion traces to the Requirement
+- [x] No PRD refs to cover
+
+---
+
+## Dependencies & Reachability
+
+**Depends on**: None
+**Entry point**: `cmd_summary`
+
+---
+
+## Acceptance Criteria
+
+| # | Criterion (testable) | Traces to requirement |
+|---|----------------------|-----------------------|
+| 1 | `summary --month 2026-03` totals only March 2026 expenses | "only count expenses dated in March 2026" |
+| 2 | `--month 2026-13` and `--month march` exit 2 with `error: ...` on stderr | "print an error and exit with status 2" |
+| 3 | `summary` without `--month` output is unchanged | "keep working exactly like it does now" |
+| 4 | Valid month with no expenses prints `No expenses.` and exits 0 | boundary (matches existing empty behavior) |
+
+---
+
+## Evaluation & Acceptance
+
+### Success Criteria
+
+| # | Given | Expect | How it's checked |
+|---|-------|--------|------------------|
+| 1 | expenses in Feb and Mar 2026; `--month 2026-03` | only March categories and total | automated test |
+| 2 | `--month 2026-13`, `--month march` | returncode 2, stderr starts `error:` | automated test |
+| 3 | no `--month` | same output as before | existing + new test |
+
+### Verification Command
+
+```bash
+python3 -m pytest tests -q
+```
+
+---
+
+## Approach
+
+**Pattern reference**: `src/tally/cli.py` `cmd_list` / `--since` (parse then filter; ValueError becomes exit 2 in `main`). `Expense.month` in `src/tally/models.py` returns "YYYY-MM".
+**Vital slice**: validate the month string (strict `YYYY-MM`, month 1–12), filter by `e.month == args.month`, in `cmd_summary` only.
+**Cut list**: no `--month` on `list`/`top`; no shorthand like `march`.
+
+Validate strictly (e.g. regex `^\d{4}-(0[1-9]|1[0-2])$` or `dt.datetime.strptime(text, "%Y-%m")` plus a length check) and raise `ValueError`. Check validity before the empty-store early return, so a bad month errors even with no expenses.
+
+## Edge Case Checklist
+
+- [ ] `2026-3` (no zero pad) rejected or consistently handled
+- [ ] `2026-13`, `2026-00`, `march`, empty string rejected
+- [ ] Bad month errors even when there are no expenses
+
+## Files to Change (Predicted)
+
+| File | Change |
+|------|--------|
+| `src/tally/cli.py` | `--month` arg + filter in `cmd_summary` |
+| `tests/test_cli.py` | new tests |
+
+## Files Must NOT Touch
+
+| File | Reason |
+|------|--------|
+| `src/tally/reports.py`, `storage.py` | out of scope |
+
+## Test Plan
+
+Add tests in `tests/test_cli.py` next to the `--since` tests, using the existing `tally` fixture.
+
+## Completion Checklist
+
+- [ ] Implementation done
+- [ ] Tests written AND pass
+- [ ] Supervisor notified: ready for Stage 4 review
